# Base URL of the Django REST API.
# Examples: https://api.seasonscake.example, https://api.seasonscake.example/api,
#           http://127.0.0.1:8010  (the client appends /api/v1 unless already present)
#
# Leave empty to run against the clearly-labelled local demo adapter (browser localStorage).
# In API mode there is no fallback to demo data: API/network errors are shown to the user.
#
# API mode notes:
# - Sign in with a real backend account (seed accounts use the SEED_PASSWORD you chose).
# - The JWT pair is kept in localStorage under "seasons-cake.tokens.v1" and revoked on sign-out.
# - The Django server must allow this origin in CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS; it must also expose
#   the "Idempotency-Key" request header (see backend/.env.example).
VITE_API_BASE_URL=
